   "notes": "Crisp chocolate wafers sandwiching a milky \"egg cream\" creme with popping candy. WAFERS: cream butter + sugar, beat in milk + vanilla, mix in dry. Roll 1/16 in. thin between parchment, chill 30 min, cut 2 in. rounds (48 wafers). Bake at 325\u00b0F about 14 min until dry and fully crisp; they crisp more as they cool. CREME: beat shortening, powdered sugar, milk powder, vanilla and salt until fluffy. It is water-free on purpose so the popping candy keeps its pop. Fold in popping candy last, pipe about 13 g per sandwich and sandwich gently without squishing. Assemble 1-2 days before packing and store airtight. (Retro Soda Fountain 2026; base batch = 24.)",
