   "ovenTemp": "350",
   "bakeMinutes": 10,
   "notes": "Soft, cakey, tart lime cookie with a sharp sour glaze, the bright counterpoint in the box. Rub zest into sugar; cream with butter; beat in egg, sour cream, lime juice and vanilla; mix in dry. Chill 30 min. Scoop 2 Tbsp balls. Bake at 350\u00b0F for 9-11 min until just set and not browned, so they stay soft. GLAZE: whisk powdered sugar, lime juice and citric acid. Dip tops once cool and finish with fresh zest. Mixing the citric acid into the glaze keeps it from weeping and getting sticky when mailed. Optional: a tiny drop of green gel color in the glaze for Christmas green. (Retro Soda Fountain 2026; base batch = 24.)",
